# novadeck kernel config fragment — SUBTRACTIVE: Qualcomm SoCs we do not ship
#
# Merged after trim-platforms.config (build.sh's *.config glob). arm64 defconfig builds the
# clocks, pinctrl and interconnect of every Qualcomm SoC, most of them into the Image, and
# all of them sit behind the one ARCH_QCOM gate we keep. So unlike trim-platforms.config this
# has to be a per-driver list: every line is a driver whose compatibles appear in none of the
# DTBs build.sh ships (disabled nodes counted), checked 2026-11-08 against SM8250, SM8550,
# SM8650 and SM8750. A driver can share an object with one we keep (gxclkctl-kaanapali.o is
# built by SM_GPUCC_8750 as well as the Kaanapali and Milos GPUCCs); that does not make it bound.
#
# A board on a new SoC: delete its SoC's lines here. A kernel bump that adds a SoC to defconfig
# builds its drivers again; build.sh names them (the unshipped-qcom note) so they can be added.
# Same syntax trap as trim-platforms.config: nothing may follow "is not set" on a directive line.

